-- Learning Process
The process of forward and backward propagation is repeated multiple times over the entire training dataset. Each repetition is called an epoch, and during each epoch, the network learns and improves its accuracy.

Why Understand ANN Structure?
Understanding the structure and function of ANNs helps in:

Designing Networks: Knowing how many layers and neurons to use.
Choosing Activation Functions: Selecting the right activation function can drastically improve performance.
Debugging and Improving: Identifying issues in network design and making informed adjustments.
